ion":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/25","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25/labels","id":15520464,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A7NLQ","number":25,"title":"4.8","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":345,"closed_issues":2335,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-04-13T15:59:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T08:15:08Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-08-28T17:04:05Z","updated_at":"2026-08-28T17:04:33Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122942","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122942","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122942.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122942.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nWhen compiling on Linux Arm64 with GCC with all warnings enabled, this error happens:\r\n\r\n```\r\nIn file included from /usr/include/string.h:580,\r\n                 from /usr/include/c++/15/cstring:48,\r\n                 from ./core/typedefs.h:53,\r\n                 from ./core/error/error_macros.h:40,\r\n                 from ./core/templates/local_vector.h:33,\r\n                 from drivers/gles3/storage/mesh_storage.h:35,\r\n                 from drivers/gles3/storage/mesh_storage.cpp:31:\r\nIn function 'void* memcpy(void*, const void*, size_t)',\r\n    inlined from 'virtual void GLES3::MeshStorage::mesh_add_surface(RID, const RenderingServerTypes::SurfaceData&)' at drivers/gles3/storage/mesh_storage.cpp:234:10:\r\n/usr/include/aarch64-linux-gnu/bits/string_fortified.h:29:33: error: 'void* __builtin_memcpy(void*, const void*, long unsigned int)' pointer overflow between offset 0 and size 18446744073709551612 [-Werror=array-bounds=]\r\n   29 |   return __builtin___memcpy_chk (__dest, __src, __len,\r\n      |          ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\r\n   30 |                                  __glibc_objsize0 (__dest));\r\n      |                                  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe specific array bounds pointer overflow described here is... not actually possible to occur, but GCC complains about it anyway, and for some reason only on arm64.\r\n\r\nThe fix: Instead of using `memcpy`, just use the CoW behavior of `Vector<>` directly. The comment already states this:\r\n\r\n```\r\n// Unfortunately, we need to copy the buffer, which is fine as doing a resize triggers a CoW anyway.\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nI used AI to identify the problem: I threw the stack trace at it and said fix, then I investigated myself. In this case, the basic solution in this PR is the same as what the AI generated.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122942/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122942/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}